{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "S"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 122, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing pooling on the direct input-output edge with an identity restores the valuable residual shortcut, whereas replacing a conv there loses capacity (#18 vs #17)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting the residual shortcut is more harmful than deleting a conv on edge 3, which can even help (#37,#39 vs #41)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a 3x3 conv for parameter-free pooling on the 0->2 path removes capacity and hurt strongly (#97) while other replaced ops gave small effects (#98-100)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing pooling on the input-output edge with a conv gives far larger gains than replacing skip or none (#74 vs #72,#73)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "With a skip shortcut, edge 5 is the main conv path to the output, so pooling it hurts most (#68 vs #69-71)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "A skip on edge 5 pays off when node 2 receives conv-processed features through edge 1 (#42,#44) but not when edge 1 is none or pooling (#43,#45)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "With a conv on edge 1 already feeding node 2, a skip on edge 2 adds an easy-to-optimize residual path (#82) instead of redundant or weak paths (#81,#83,#84)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 3 is also a conv, the all-conv cell is over-deep and hard to optimize, so pruning edge 4 helped (#62) while it was near-neutral otherwise (#60,#61,#63)."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without an edge-3 shortcut, removing edge 0 simplifies the cell and helped (#19,#20), whereas with a skip shortcut it was mostly harmful (#21,#23)."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Removing edge 1 was roughly neutral when edge 2 was empty (#78) but strongly negative when edge 2 carried a conv or skip (#77,#80)."}], "tok": 19908, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "none"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "avg_pool_3x3"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1"], [5, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "none", "nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "skip_connect"]], [["nor_conv_3x3